1
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and it
flies until it gets there.

3
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:29,260
Joking around with the PE teacher Kashiwa,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
they laughed at me for
staying as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow rouse
my spirits somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
there's only one way to win,
and a reason to try.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare, and the unchanging streetscape,

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
are gentler still.

9
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,900
the sun is already setting.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:52,180
Yakitori Honbari.

12
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,840
Is anyone there?

13
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat,

14
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:04,060
straight from the waterworks toward the vast sky,
the sun sets.

15
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow it will end the same way, won't it.

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,740
Again they say that's happiness, I wonder.

17
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm a fool who only
realized it by taking the easy way.

18
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:27,680
Mountains

19
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:29,540
Rivers

20
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:31,760
Flowers

21
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:35,200
and strawberry picking!

22
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:39,720
Welcome to the Chiba Flower Garden Center!

23
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,120
Director, it's perfect!

24
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:45,860
Alright, let's use that in our ads.

25
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:48,020
We'll blast commercials on TV nonstop!

26
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:49,240
Harui-kun

27
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,480
What's the schedule for
today's group visitors?

28
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:53,820
Yes, please wait a moment.

29
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:55,831
Well,

30
00:01:55,881 --> 00:01:59,216
this morning,
the children from Tanpopo Kindergarten,

31
00:01:59,266 --> 00:02:02,080
the Himawari Nursing Home group, and also...

32
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:05,040
I was told there were only
two groups in the morning?

33
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,660
Well, a reservation came
in suddenly yesterday.

34
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,280
And what place is this, may I ask?

35
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:12,400
It's the Katsushika police station in Tokyo.

36
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:13,600
What?!

37
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,020
W-what's with the sudden fuss?

38
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,100
It's coming!

39
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:18,400
That man is...!

40
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:19,900
A-again!

41
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,700
He's coming to our place again!

42
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:30,160
This is the men's strawberry picking!

43
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:35,880
the strawberries we lovingly grew

44
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:38,240
devoured them like a black hole.

45
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:40,060
That man is coming.

46
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:41,480
That man? Who?

47
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:44,160
Right, you newcomers

48
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:46,000
don't you know about that man?

49
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,780
Just thinking about him is terrifying.

50
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:52,140
Welcome to the Hanabatake Garden Center!

51
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:53,480
Nice to meet you.

52
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,280
We're in your care.

53
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:57,000
It's milk.

54
00:02:57,420 --> 00:02:59,320
Please take one each.

55
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,800
This way, please.

56
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:07,960
These strawberries are small and cute.

57
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,460
Really.

58
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:10,860
But they're not red yet,

59
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:13,260
so let's save them for the next customers.

60
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,800
Alright.

61
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,380
Ankichi.

62
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:18,620
Red or green, a snack's a snack.

63
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:19,760
That's awful.

64
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:20,620
What kind of person does that?

65
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:23,120
Please,
go ahead and eat as much as you like.

66
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:25,440
So we can really eat as much as we want?

67
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:28,540
Of course. All-you-can-eat, no takeaway.

68
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,680
Alright, got it.

69
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:31,120
It's delicious!

70
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:32,440
Come on, go ahead.

71
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:32,940
Slurp.

72
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:34,980
Visitors.

73
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:37,600
Gulp, not bad at all. Next.

74
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:39,700
No way.

75
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:40,700
What are you doing?

76
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:45,000
That guy's a wily one.

77
00:03:45,780 --> 00:03:47,060
What, you beast!

78
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:50,040
That's not quite right, is it.

79
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:51,700
This is how you eat fruit!

80
00:03:54,360 --> 00:04:00,540
W-what was that?

81
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:06,980
It was truly a nightmare.
That guy is an absolute monster.

82
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:10,300
He ate up an entire greenhouse.
Well, not all of it, but he ate plenty.

83
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:12,840
Not even a blade of grass was left behind.

84
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:15,800
So that's why there's a
notice like this posted.

85
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:18,220
Things no normal person
would ever think of, right?

86
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:21,060
Still, that man might
just do it again this year.

87
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:21,547
Everyone,

88
00:04:21,597 --> 00:04:25,180
for the strawberries and
fruit we've lovingly grown,

89
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:27,740
we will definitely get revenge on that man!

90
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:28,460
Yeah!

91
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:33,460
H-here he comes!

92
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:38,580
W-welcome!

93
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:42,160
Alright, everyone,
please take a container and some milk.

94
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,620
W-welcome!

95
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:46,400
Please only pick the red strawberries, okay?

96
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,020
Yes, coming!

97
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:48,920
Right this way, right this way.

98
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:52,540
I was having such a nice nap, honestly.

99
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:54,900
You sleep too much, senpai.

100
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,100
Welcome!

101
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:58,440
Happy New Year to you, too.

102
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,880
Yes, we've been waiting for you!

103
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,640
Here he comes!

104
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,980
Excuse me, this way, please.

105
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,400
Everyone's over here!

106
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:16,400
Yes, that house is for women
and people who don't eat much.

107
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:21,180
Since you all look like
you have big appetites,

108
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,800
Well, I'm not really

109
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:23,840
That's right.

110
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:25,900
We're dying to eat some strawberries!

111
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:28,940
I skipped three days of meals for this day.

112
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:30,440
I thought so.

113
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:32,360
For people like that,

114
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:36,100
we also have a house where you can
eat especially large strawberries.

115
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:38,440
Well, aren't you prepared.

116
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:40,160
Where's that house?

117
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:41,960
Yes, it's over that way.

118
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:44,920
Now I can get revenge on
that guy who tricked us.

119
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,680
Everyone who's hungry,

120
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:50,000
help yourselves to as many
sweet strawberries as you like.

121
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:50,920
Yay!

122
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,560
Hey, where's the strawberry?

123
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:59,160
It's just a cucumber painted red!

124
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:01,120
What are you talking about?

125
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:04,720
This is a genuine,
brand-new variety of Asian strawberry.

126
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:08,180
But no matter how you look at it,
it's a red cucumber.

127
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:11,040
It's three times tastier
than a regular strawberry.

128
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:13,320
Think of it as being tricked.
Please just try eating one.

129
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:14,080
Well then,

130
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:15,840
Hey, get back here!

131
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,640
We're not kappa, you know!

132
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,540
Senpai, just try eating it, come on.

133
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,220
Fine, I guess there's no choice.

134
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:30,020
This flavor really is cucumber, after all.

135
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:32,100
It doesn't go well with milk, does it?

136
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:34,120
This goes much better with miso!

137
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:36,180
Go get some Honda miso.

138
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:36,780
Yes.

139
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:41,480
Delicious.

140
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:43,060
Miso really does go well with it!

141
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:44,420
It's like moro-kyu, isn't it.

142
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:46,480
Save some for me, okay?

143
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:57,380
Ate it all! Where's the next strawberry house?
Okay, you're not planning to feed us another weird new variety in the next house, are you?

144
00:06:57,880 --> 00:07:08,440
No, this time it's jumbo strawberries, each one weighing a full kilo!
Hey, senpai, we can handle this one, right? Alright, we'll devour the jumbo strawberries too!

145
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:12,100
I wonder about that.

146
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:12,860
Yeah.

147
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:26,220
It's red, but it's a pumpkin, right? Even if you paint it,
there's no way the inside tastes like strawberries.

148
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:31,440
First that cucumber, and now that director...
what's he thinking? Well.

149
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:40,300
Aaah, I get it now! That old man's
here for revenge for last year!

150
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:43,040
I have a plan.

151
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:48,000
Wow, painting a pumpkin red and calling it a jumbo strawberry,
what a idea.

152
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,080
Even that guy can't eat
a hard pumpkin, can he?

153
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:53,780
This time,
we're getting our revenge for sure!

154
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:57,780
Senpai, what's your plan?

155
00:07:58,280 --> 00:08:01,640
Listen, didn't the director
say to go to the next house over?

156
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:05,060
Past that Asian house is
the jumbo strawberries, and

157
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:07,000
This one's the neighboring house too, right?

158
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:07,460
Yes.

159
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:09,820
Look at this.

160
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:10,100
Ta-da!

161
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:11,600
Look, look!

162
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:12,440
Why?

163
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:15,640
Whoa! It's a melon!

164
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:20,180
Look, each one weighs a full kilo!

165
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:23,360
These are definitely the
real jumbo strawberries.

166
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,320
Hey, Honda.

167
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:25,620
Yeah, you're right.

168
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:28,320
Alright, let's eat!

169
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:33,840
Looks delicious.

170
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,560
This is good!

171
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:39,780
Hey, jumbo strawberries taste like melon

172
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:44,300
They're probably bred to taste like melon.

173
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:50,460
W-what, I have a bad feeling about this.

174
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:51,998
Director, am I imagining things, or

175
00:08:52,048 --> 00:08:54,520
I hear voices coming from the melon house.

176
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:55,543
No way,

177
00:08:55,593 --> 00:09:00,980
those are top-grade melons we
raised one by one with loving care!

178
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:03,720
Each one fetches ten thousand yen, you know.

179
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:06,760
Of course. This year's melons
are the best we've ever grown.

180
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:08,720
If anything happens to them...

181
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:12,640
No way.

182
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:15,360
Hey, what are you doing?

183
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:18,460
Director,
those really were delicious strawberries.

184
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:18,800
What?

185
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,200
This is -

186
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:28,440
the melons I poured my heart into growing,

187
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,640
those guys are eating them!

188
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:34,340
Aww! That melon I mean,
those strawberries were tasty

189
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:39,080
You lot! How dare you devour
everyone's melons like that!

190
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:43,060
Those weren't jumbo strawberries, were they?

191
00:09:43,060 --> 00:09:48,680
What strawberries?! Those are melons that cost ten thousand yen each!
You gobbled up every last one!

192
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:52,170
But you said it was the next house over,

193
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:54,860
and you said it was about this big,

194
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:59,320
and it weighed about the same,
so I got mixed up.

195
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:01,360
Nori!

196
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:04,160
Well, now that we've
eaten up this house too,

197
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,900
you'll let us eat at
the next house too, right?

198
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:09,480
F-fine, I'll let you eat them.

199
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:12,940
I've been thinking I'd
have to fight you someday.

200
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:14,760
Now that's interesting.

201
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:16,420
Think you can beat me?

202
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:25,800
In this tropical house,

203
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:27,739
bananas, papayas,

204
00:10:27,789 --> 00:10:30,220
mangoes, pineapples,

205
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:33,600
and the king of fruits, durian,

206
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:37,417
and many other tropical fruits.

207
00:10:37,467 --> 00:10:38,920
All you can eat.

208
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:39,812
But,

209
00:10:39,862 --> 00:10:43,160
that's only if you can make
it all the way over there.

210
00:10:45,260 --> 00:10:47,880
Well, that's an interesting way of thinking.

211
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:50,020
Volvo, get the rope out.

212
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:57,540
Okay, okay, you're fine, right?

213
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:01,360
We take no responsibility whatsoever
for accidents inside the greenhouse.

214
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,500
Is that really all right with you?

215
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:03,300
Sure, it's fine.

216
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,500
That's ridiculous.

217
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:12,560
What a man.

218
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,160
Hey, Honda!

219
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:15,880
I'll haul you up.

220
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:17,760
Tie yourself to that rope.

221
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:18,880
Yes.

222
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:21,620
Hey, you.

223
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,860
Director, are you really all right?

224
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:30,320
We still have plenty
of plans up our sleeves.

225
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:35,740
Don't underestimate Kankichi Ryotsu-sama!

226
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,500
Enjoy talking big while you still can.

227
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:02,560
Face?

228
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:03,640
What?

229
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:05,720
It's true.

230
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:08,080
There's loads of fruit over there.

231
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:10,900
So we're supposed to cross here

232
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:13,240
What should we do, swim over?

233
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:14,880
That's impossible!

234
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:18,960
Alright, leave it to me.

235
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:28,060
This should be good enough.

236
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:37,280
With this,
we'll get the fruit in this house too.

237
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:43,160
Alright, just a little more...
but we'll get busted!

238
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:48,600
Whoa, hey, Senpai, what are you...

239
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:49,100
What?!

240
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:55,600
W-why is there a crocodile
in the greenhouse?!

241
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:02,680
Hahaha, what's the matter, sir?

242
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:05,880
You're not going to give up here, are you?!

243
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:07,520
Old man!

244
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:10,840
If it comes to this, I'll swim across!

245
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:11,720
Hmph!

246
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:52,160
What are you talking about?

247
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:53,120
I can't say anything.

248
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:53,740
Okay.

249
00:13:53,740 --> 00:13:54,120
No way.

250
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:55,800
Stop it!

251
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:56,880
Okay, I've got it.

252
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:00,940
Why me?

253
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,740
Why me?

254
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:06,140
Why me?

255
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:08,040
Why me?

256
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:15,480
Way to go, Onda!

257
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:16,600
Hurry up and get on.

258
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:18,960
Heave-ho!

259
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:22,940
Okay, hold on tight.

260
00:14:25,820 --> 00:14:26,260
Okay.

261
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,580
Here I go!

262
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:33,460
Throw the rope!

263
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:41,880
Next move.

264
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:06,460
So sweet.

265
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,640
We ate and ate.

266
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:19,120
Fruit after a hard day's work is the best.

267
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:19,920
Totally.

268
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,740
We must have crossed the river.

269
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:25,180
Come to think of it,
we haven't seen any durian.

270
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:29,880
Enjoy!

271
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:33,480
The durian is over there.

272
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:34,860
A waterfall?

273
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:36,500
That's right.

274
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:39,220
The durian house is above that waterfall.

275
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:42,520
Over there, the king of fruits, durian...

276
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:49,440
It's not that big a waterfall.

277
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:50,940
Right.

278
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:55,440
Climb this waterfall, and I'll lower
a rope from the top, so follow me.

279
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:56,080
Okay.

280
00:15:56,820 --> 00:15:58,280
Climb the waterfall?

281
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:02,360
What?

282
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:08,540
Okay.

283
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:12,016
Alright,

284
00:16:12,066 --> 00:16:19,120
I tied it to the rock!

285
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:21,280
Hold onto that rope and come across!

286
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:22,440
Don't fall!

287
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,000
Okay!

288
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:50,520
Nnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnn...

289
00:17:00,780 --> 00:17:03,020
They're throwing durians into the water.

290
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:06,820
What?

291
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:14,640
What is it?

292
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:22,700
Durian, durian,
Rocky's girlfriend is Adrian.

293
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:25,440
Gyuroro borobororobo!

294
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:27,960
What are they doing?

295
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:30,640
Are they doing synchronized
swimming or something?

296
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:45,520
Delicious.

297
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:47,380
This one doesn't stink.

298
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:49,900
As expected of a king's taste.

299
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:53,340
But my breath stinks.

300
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:58,180
Arian do aia

301
00:17:58,180 --> 00:18:01,760
Rocky's guard is "eido aia"

302
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:04,940
In the water, it'll stink even more.

303
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:16,200
Come to think of it,
we haven't eaten the strawberries yet.

304
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:17,680
That's right.

305
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,280
Give me the strawberries to eat.

306
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:21,100
Right, feed me!

307
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:24,060
Alright, I'll feed you!

308
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:27,020
Real strawberries, plenty of them!

309
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:29,220
The pinnacle of strawberries!

310
00:18:29,220 --> 00:18:31,700
It's a strawberry tablet, 500 yen a piece!

311
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:33,820
I'll make you eat this!

312
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:37,740
Here, here, here, here, here,
here, here, here, here, here, here!

313
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:38,680
Director?

314
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:39,520
What?

315
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:40,940
Come on.

316
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:44,640
Director, let's stop already.

317
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,580
It's far too dangerous.

318
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:48,160
Shut up, this is revenge!

319
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:54,960
What are you doing?

320
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:57,820
Come on, if you can eat it,
go ahead and try!

321
00:18:57,820 --> 00:19:00,440
Hurry up, or it'll burn out!

322
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:05,000
What a guy!

323
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:06,500
Sepoi

324
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:12,680
Senpai, n-no way!

325
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:13,820
Y-you're going in?

326
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:16,260
Let's dig in!

327
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:16,900
No way?

328
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:22,440
Everyone, what's wrong?

329
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:23,960
Senpai is in there!

330
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:25,280
Ryo-chan's in there?

331
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:28,100
Wh-what a heat!

332
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:30,060
No time to dip it in milk!

333
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:32,960
No, some of the strawberries are burnt too.

334
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,520
Hey, senpai!

335
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:39,800
Ryo-chan!

336
00:19:43,120 --> 00:20:00,120
Aaaaaahhh hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot
hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot!

337
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:01,480
Hah! Let go!

338
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:03,380
This time, it's a real showdown!

339
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:05,820
I accept that challenge!

340
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:11,280
The ultimate fruit,
made with biotech-grown water!

341
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:14,280
Eat all the Rainbow Watermelon you want!

342
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:16,040
What? It's just a watermelon?

343
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:17,980
Don't underestimate me.

344
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:26,100
It's a rainbow watermelon!

345
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:30,920
What is this watermelon?

346
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:37,480
Strawberry, watermelon, orange,
banana, melon, kiwi all in one,

347
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:40,560
grape: a superb fruit where
you can enjoy seven flavors.

348
00:20:40,560 --> 00:20:41,420
Amazing!

349
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:42,860
It looks delicious.

350
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:44,280
Seven flavors

351
00:20:44,280 --> 00:20:46,120
Alright, everyone, let's eat!

352
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:48,080
What?

353
00:20:49,380 --> 00:20:51,620
What's this?

354
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:58,000
A lion!

355
00:20:58,980 --> 00:21:02,760
If we press this switch,
the fence in front of it opens too,

356
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:07,580
so we can enjoy rainbow watermelon
hunting alongside the lion!

357
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:09,620
I see.

358
00:21:09,620 --> 00:21:12,900
Fruit hunting with a lion isn't bad, either.

359
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:17,540
But the rainbow watermelon
alone is a bit too risky.

360
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:22,360
If only they'd scatter some cash too.

361
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:24,180
What? Cash?

362
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:26,320
Yeah, cash.

363
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:28,460
M-money's a bit...

364
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:34,000
What? We're risking our lives here,
and you don't want to pay any money?

365
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:36,748
Just as I thought,

366
00:21:36,798 --> 00:21:40,080
your own money matters more than someone's life,
doesn't it?

367
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:40,740
Hey,

368
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:42,897
Director,

369
00:21:42,947 --> 00:21:46,480
Don't fall for the provocation.

370
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:48,520
Alright, let's do it!

371
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:49,500
Just you wait.

372
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:52,540
Director.

373
00:21:56,880 --> 00:21:59,480
5 million yen in secret
savings I hid from my wife.

374
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:01,080
I'll give it all to you.

375
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:09,740
But in return, the time limit is 30 minutes.

376
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:19,580
Enjoy yourselves.

377
00:22:21,580 --> 00:22:24,300
Reiko-san, aren't you going to stop them?

378
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:26,340
There's no need to worry.

379
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:29,280
The outcome is already clear
once the money is on the table.

380
00:22:38,740 --> 00:22:41,700
Gone quiet... no way, Senpai?

381
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:43,960
Hey, pull me up!

382
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:51,980
That took a little longer than expected.

383
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:53,920
Senpai.

384
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:57,040
The lion bit off about
100,000 yen's worth, but

385
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:59,200
we got the rest of them!

386
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:07,200
We got to do some great strawberry picking!

387
00:23:12,300 --> 00:23:13,720
Time's up.

388
00:23:14,440 --> 00:23:17,640
Anything not fully picked,
we'll have to take back.

389
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:18,520
What?

390
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:20,540
Too bad.

391
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,680
Please come again next year.

392
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:23,840
Oh well, there's nothing to be done.

393
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:24,660
Ryo-chan.

394
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:26,640
Make sure you clean up after yourselves.

395
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:28,160
Excuse me, I'll be going ahead.

396
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:30,820
Wait a minute, you guys!

397
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:35,280
You're really leaving?

398
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:36,560
Hey, wait!

399
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:39,920
Don't leave me behind!

400
00:23:47,380 --> 00:23:50,420
It sounds like someone is calling

401
00:23:51,060 --> 00:23:52,980
on an afternoon after the rain.

402
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:59,600
Walking and looking back,
led along by the gacha-gacha.

403
00:24:00,660 --> 00:24:06,780
That strange feeling I had back then.

404
00:24:07,460 --> 00:24:12,020
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

405
00:24:12,020 --> 00:24:17,780
I walked only on the black ones.

406
00:24:20,300 --> 00:24:25,940
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

407
00:24:27,060 --> 00:24:33,420
Even the politicians with their pompous
faces and the aunties with blue eyeshadow.

408
00:24:33,940 --> 00:24:44,180
Turn that corner over there and you'll meet everyone,
you'll see everyone.

409
00:24:44,180 --> 00:24:52,160
Over there is Kame surely there is Kame.

410
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:57,480
Come on, everyone, to our town.

411
00:24:57,480 --> 00:25:05,300
Over there is Kame surely there is Kame.

412
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:10,580
Come on, everyone, to our town.

413
00:25:15,780 --> 00:25:16,820
What's going on?

414
00:25:16,820 --> 00:25:19,400
An ostrich is running wild all over town!

415
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:20,940
Just catch it, whatever it takes!

416
00:25:20,940 --> 00:25:23,360
All officers from the Kameari Park police box,
dispatch now!

417
00:25:23,360 --> 00:25:26,140
So I have to catch it all by myself?

418
00:25:26,140 --> 00:25:28,540
That's impossible, impossible, impossible!

419
00:25:28,540 --> 00:25:31,200
Next time, Mr. Ostrich, come visit.

420
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:32,100
Nice to meet you.

421
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:35,920
Over there is Kameari.

422
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:39,260
Well, surely it's Kameari.

423
00:25:40,360 --> 00:25:44,280
Everyone, come on over to our town!

424
00:25:45,140 --> 00:25:45,840
Thank you.

